course: dictionary
lesson: 6460
title: NASA
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: NASA is a name for an organisation, so it begins with a capital letter. It is an acronym, which means its name is made from the first letters of longer words: National Aeronautics and Space Administration. People say it as one word, «NAS-uh».
explain: NASA is the space agency of the United States. It is a clue when you see phrases like NASA scientists, a NASA mission or NASA astronauts: the word tells you who is doing the job and that it is about space.
explain: Read the sentence around the word. «NASA's Dragonfly, a drone-like rotorcraft due to launch around 2028, is planned to fly in the thick air of Saturn's moon Titan in the 2030s.» The words launch, fly and Titan show you that NASA is working on a space mission, so you can work out the meaning from the context.
fact: NASA stands for National Aeronautics and Space Administration.
fact: NASA is the space agency of the United States.
fact: NASA sends astronauts, rockets and probes into space.
fact: «NASA's Dragonfly» is a drone-like rotorcraft planned to fly on Saturn's moon Titan in the 2030s.
fact: NASA's Apollo missions used a lunar orbit route calculated by Yuri Kondratiuk.
exercise: «NASA's Dragonfly is due to launch around 2028.» What is NASA? | A pizza shop in Florida | *A space agency of the United States | A school for astronauts | A type of rocket fuel from the sea
exercise: Ella says NASA is a word for any space rock. What is the right meaning? | Any rock that falls from the sky | A planet near the Sun | A kind of space suit | *The space agency of the United States, which sends astronauts and rockets into space
exercise: «NASA astronauts flew to the Moon.» Find and copy one word that is a clue that the sentence is about space. | Moon | the | flew | *astronauts
exercise: Which words in «NASA's Dragonfly, a drone-like rotorcraft due to launch around 2028, is planned to fly on Titan» tell you it is a space mission? | due and planned | *launch and Titan | drone and fly | around and 2028
test: What do the letters in NASA stand for? | National Air and Sea Authority | North American Space Agency | *National Aeronautics and Space Administration | New Astronomy Study Academy
test: What is an acronym? | *A word made from the first letters of longer words | A word that means the same as another word | A long word for a planet | A word that is always spelled with a capital letter
exam: Jayden reads «NASA scientists» and asks what it means. What is the best answer? | Scientists who only work in hospitals | *Scientists who work for NASA, the space agency of the United States | Scientists who study fish in the sea | Any scientist who likes the Moon
